{"name":"Decor Yellow","hex":"#f6bb00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"decor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The style of decoration of a room or building.","A stage setting; scenery; set; backdrop."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decor"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Interior design","blocks":[{"text":"Interior design is the art and science of enhancing the interior of a building to achieve a healthier and more aesthetically pleasing environment for the people using the space. With a keen eye for detail and a creative flair, an interior designer is someone who plans, researches, coordinates, and manages such enhancement projects. Interior design is a multifaceted profession that includes conceptual development, space planning, site inspections, programming, research, communicating with the stakeholders of a project, construction management, and execution of the design. Interior designers make use of fundamental design principles from the visual arts used to help viewers understand a given scene."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/30th_Street_Station_concourse_looking_west_July_2026.jpeg/330px-30th_Street_Station_concourse_looking_west_July_2026.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interior_design"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG/500px-Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG/1280px-Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG/500px-Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The lobby of Hotel Bristol, Warsaw","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg/500px-Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign